  "notes": "Definition: c_lambda(q) := s_lambda(1, q, ..., q^{n_strands-1}) = principal q-specialisation of the Schur polynomial = Macdonald hook-content formula = Demazure character D_{w_0}(lambda) at x_i := q^{i-1} (verified by demazure-markov-trace witness). At q -> 1 this equals dim V_lambda for sl_n = |B(lambda, n)| from crystal_basis.crystal_B (Weyl dimension formula). We report BOTH the q-deformed (q_0) and the q -> 1 variants, since AGENTS.md sec.7b shortcut #3 leaves the choice open for the symmetric-crystal case (the Type-B fold-orbit closure work uses crystal *cardinality* at q=1, while the Demazure-fiber Markov-trace functional uses the q-deformed character).",
  "honest_reporting": "Per protocol: c_lambda is NOT scaled to force the mass equation to close. The residual (target - sum) and the diagnostic scalar alpha_E (the would-close-it factor) are both reported. If alpha_E differs significantly from 1, the Kashiwara crystal weights are NOT the correct closed form for Delta_lambda; a flat-transport correction (q -> 0 -> q_0 connection curvature, per rem:ontological-agnosticism) would have to make up the difference, OR a different structural weight (Plancherel-truncated, jet-knot, ...) applies.",
  "follow_up": "If option E shows |alpha_E - 1| << 1 (close to closure), extend to (T, 3He) at n=9 and 4He at n=12. If alpha_E is far from 1, compare the residual to the four other options (A: crystal-truncated minimum-norm, B: Plancherel bound, C: jet-knot Hochschild, D: Type-B fold-orbit projection) in the parent PR #600 brief; the smallest residual wins.",
